{"seq":18,"trial_id":"installer-cc-codex-acl-2026-11/claude-code-opus-gbrain-told-acl-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-03T15:34:28.237Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"34afc7ac2d9856c0c69015e9ad7ff53e6c1666ec8610ef98265fc12aaf910dca","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DINSTAL0001","text":"Hi Dana, I checked all six of Moss's notes in the shared files. Two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers come up:\n\n• *#PD-4492*: from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md, 5 Oct 2025). Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers at Dock Doors 14–18 in Eau Claire weren't getting SMS bay assignments at the gatehouse kiosk. Support patched it at 19:30 that evening, and Thea confirmed the 04:00 shift on 5 Oct got through the gate without help. The note's action item was to archive the Eau Claire kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n• *#4419*: from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It's been escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing.\n\nTwo things to check before this goes in the weekly notes:\n• #4419 also appears in Marcus's own note \"Q2 expansion wrap\" (14 Jul 2025), which isn't one of Moss's. There it's described as \"Gate 3 printer lag\", a BOL printout delay that had been patched. That doesn't match Moss's scanner description, so it's worth confirming against the ticket itself.\n• The cheat sheet has no date, so I can't say how current the #4419 status is.\n\nMoss's two Central notes also list tickets #4409 and #4412, but those belong to Pree's dealer account, not QFL, so I left them out."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DINSTAL0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
